      "text": "June 14, 2025 | Daily Crypto + Macro Rundown\n\n1-Market Pulse\nTotal crypto market cap dips 4% to $3.51T after a short-term rally. Trading volume remains high at $132B. Volatility persists, but activity stays strong.\n\n2-Memecoin Spotlight\nNo major launches today, but attention stays on earlier 2025 entries like $TRUMP, $SNORT, $MooDeng, and $MEW. Memecoins still dominate sentiment and speculative flows.\n\n3-$TRUMP Breakdown\nOnce a top 20 token, $TRUMP is down 85% from its $75 ATH. A $520M unlock on July 18 looms large. Trump family still holds 80%, valued at $3B+. Ethics controversy continues to grow.\n\n4- $SNORT Token\nLaunched May 29, Snorter mixes humor with utility via Telegram trading tools. Raised $167K in 24h. Popular, but long-term outlook unclear.\n\n5- $MooDeng & $MEW Momentum:\nRobinhood listing on May 22 spiked visibility. Pro-crypto policy shifts under Trump are fueling retail excitement. Both remain social trend-driven.\n\n6- What’s Brewing\nhttps://t.co/XQPSq7zCSd is evolving—launching its own memecoin after acting as a Solana launchpad. Meanwhile, ZORO drops AI-on-Chain tools on BNB, hinting at AI-memecoin hybrids.\n\n7-Regulatory Watch\nSenate Dems push back on political crypto profiteering—aimed directly at $TRUMP. Trump admin continues pro-crypto stance, creating tension with regulatory agencies.\n\n8-Corporate Moves\nAmazon and Walmart are reportedly exploring USD-backed stablecoins. Big Tech’s slow but steady move into crypto continues.\n\n9-Red Flags\nA €3M NFT scam tied to footballer Papu Gómez reignites concerns over celebrity-endorsed projects. Memecoins remain high-risk, high-reward.\n\n8-Key Date Ahead\n\nWatch June 27 EveryX's private launch in Quezon City could unveil fresh Web3 projects and memecoin crossovers.\n\njoin https://t.co/EMuRv9dgyU to get complete minshare breakdown",
